  <section class="join" id="join" aria-labelledby="signup-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card">
        <div>
          <h2 id="signup-heading">Join the Edinburgh Tours list</h2>
          <p class="intro">Leave your email and first name to hear about new walks. First-time guests also receive an introductory offer.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <form id="signup">
            <div class="fields">
              <div class="field">
                <label>Email <input type="email" id="email" required autocomplete="email"></label>
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label>First name <input type="text" id="first_name" required maxlength="50" autocomplete="given-name"></label>
              </div>
            </div>
            <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
          </form>
          <p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="route-section" id="route" aria-labelledby="route-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="route-heading">The route</h2>
        <p>The walk covers five stops in the old city, with a rest landing on the longest stairway and a short pause at the end. All stop names are invented for this fictional tour.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="route">
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Lantern Gate</strong>
            <span>Your guide greets the group, shares the plan for the afternoon and hands out a printed route map.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>The Winding Stair</strong>
            <span>A curving stairway between tall tenements, with a handrail and a rest landing halfway up.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Quill Court</strong>
            <span>A sheltered courtyard that once housed printers and bookbinders, who left their marks on the walls.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Merchant&rsquo;s Pend</strong>
            <span>A covered passage where your guide explains how the old closes earned their names.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>The Lookout Yard</strong>
            <span>A small terrace above the rooftops, where the walk ends with a quiet pause and time for questions.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="visit" id="visit" aria-labelledby="visit-heading">
    <div class="wrap visit-grid">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="visit-heading">Good to know</h2>
        <p>The Hidden Closes Stroll suits anyone who enjoys an unhurried afternoon. Your guide adjusts the pace to the group and keeps an eye out for anyone who needs a rest.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/" aria-label="Book now: Hidden Closes Stroll">Book now</a>
      </div>

      <dl class="panel">
        <div>
          <dt>When</dt>
          <dd>Wednesday at 2:00 pm.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Length</dt>
          <dd>About two hours, including two rest stops.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Pace</dt>
